gupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/76cd16bfe4567ad0341a8e2107c6f286a057f37a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:02:02Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:02:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: steady period changes, animated landing page, border and theme fixes (2.28.0) (#259)\n\n* feat: steady period changes, animated landing page, border and theme fixes, enforced 50/30/20 split\n\nAnalytics pages keep the last consistent figures on screen while a new\nperiod loads, so they never collapse to a skeleton or mix ranges. The\nlanding page gains an animated sample money-flow, KPIs and chart without\nloading recharts. Border utilities apply again after moving global border\nrules into cascade layers, theme colors follow a toggle on goals,\ncomparison, budget and anomalies, needs/wants/savings must total 100%,\nand a nullable recurring user amount column lands as phase 1 of making\nedited recurring amounts stick. Release 2.28.0.\n\n* feat: typescript 7 and theme-following chart colors\n\nCharts that copied palette hex at import or inside a memo kept the old\ntheme after a toggle on six pages. A usePaletteSnapshot hook hands those\nmemos a palette copy that changes on every theme refresh, the remaining\nmodule constants rebuild in place, and the Year in Review heatmap now\nuses var() with color-mix. tsc runs TypeScript 7; a pnpmfile hook keeps\ntypescript-eslint on its own TypeScript 6 because TS 7 ships no JS API.\nAlso makes the landing page label spacing explicit for Sonar S6772.","tree":{"sha":"b7ae0b5b8859c14a1c686592cdd7a53d4d8e465b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/b7ae0b5b8859c14a1c686592cdd7a53d4d8e465b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/76cd16bfe4567ad0341a8e2107c6f286a057f37a","verification":{"payload":"tree b7ae0b5b8859c14a1c686592cdd7a53d4d8e465b\nparent 2291525d1212e9194d1804875f7b71d9390237ba\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1791421322 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791421322 +0530\n\nfeat: steady period changes, animated landing page, border and theme fixes (2.28.0) (#259)\n\n* feat: steady period changes, animated landing page, border and theme fixes, enforced 50/30/20 split\n\nAnalytics pages keep the last consistent figures on screen while a new\nperiod loads, so they never collapse to a skeleton or mix ranges. The\nlanding page gains an animated sample money-flow, KPIs and chart without\nloading recharts. Border utilities apply again after moving global border\nrules into cascade layers, theme colors follow a toggle on goals,\ncomparison, budget and anomalies, needs/wants/savings must total 100%,\nand a nullable recurring user amount column lands as phase 1 of making\nedited recurring amounts stick. Release 2.28.0.\n\n* feat: typescript 7 and theme-following chart colors\n\nCharts that copied palette hex at import or inside a memo kept the old\ntheme after a toggle on six pages. A usePaletteSnapshot hook hands those\nmemos a palette copy that changes on every theme refresh, the remaining\nmodule constants rebuild in place, and the Year in Review heatmap now\nuses var() with color-mix. tsc runs TypeScript 7; a pnpmfile hook keeps\ntypescript-eslint on its own TypeScript 6 because TS 7 ships no JS API.\nAlso makes the landing page label spacing explicit for Sonar S6772.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxuuKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAgUQAGQcYKw33aFNrWxv8vEDZbDP\nJDH+QdigYEYSzi