"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/08c9d0337933037712b2aa4c1a1688f304274ad9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:01:21Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:01:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(db): move account, AI, and compensation settings into domain tables (#250)\n\nStructured preferences lived as JSON blobs in TEXT columns on\n`user_preferences`, so nothing could be queried, constrained, or indexed.\nAccount classifications, AI provider configuration, and salary/RSU/growth\ninputs were all opaque strings the API parsed on every read.\n\nGives three domain areas real relational storage: `_models/compensation.py`\nplus `services/compensation.py` for salary components, RSU grants and vesting\nrows, and growth assumptions; `_models/ai_settings.py` plus\n`services/ai_settings.py` for provider, model, key envelope and token budgets;\nand `services/account_settings.py` for account classification. Consumers were\nrepointed at the new tables: query_helpers, anomalies, net_worth, recurring,\ntrends, the AI tool implementations, the preferences routers, auth_service and\nledger_dimensions.\n\nFour chained revisions land it, ending in an explicit cutover:\naccount_settings_2026, ai_settings_2026, compensation_records_2026, then\ndomain_storage_cutover_2026. The chain resolves to exactly one head across all\n55 revisions, and CI now runs the new migration tests in the PostgreSQL\nintegration job, because a dialect difference passes on SQLite and fails in\nproduction.\n\nDocuments the result in docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA_REFERENCE.md, a JSON companion,\nand a DDL snapshot, with the design and verification notes under docs/plans/\nand docs/research/.\n\nAlso fixes the schema reference''s provenance record. As a path-keyed map,\n`source_files_sha256` paired a credential-looking key with a high-entropy value\nwhenever the path contained auth or token, so SonarCloud reported seven BLOCKER\nhard-coded-secret findings and an E security rating. The values are file\ndigests, confirmed by recomputing sha256 over auth_service.py. Restructured to\na list of {path, sha256} objects, verified lossless across all 129 pairs.\n\nGitignores backend/.pytest_tmp/, the scratch SQLite directory the new\nmigration tests build, which was untracked but unignored.\n\nVerified: 1585 backend tests pass with 205 skipped, ruff and mypy clean, and\nthe Sonar gate green with security rating A and zero vulnerabilities.","tree":{"sha":"8a73a2b9818b5cd589c2c627df9c4fc6160e3efb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/8a73a2b9818b5cd589c2c627df9c4fc6160e3efb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/08c9d0337933037712b2aa4c1a1688f304274ad9","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a73a2b9818b5cd589c2c627df9c4fc6160e3efb\nparent 8768a147347ff0576060926cc3bd7f3d68fd4e20\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1789693281 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789693281 +0530\n\nfeat(db): move account, AI, and compensation settings into domain tables (#250)\n\nStructured preferences lived as JSON blobs in TEXT columns on\n`user_preferences`, so nothing could be queried, constrained, or indexed.\nAccount classifications, AI provider configuration, and salary/RSU/growth\ninputs were all opaque strings the API parsed on every read.\n\nGives three domain areas real relational storage: `_models/compensation.py`\nplus `services/compensation.py` for salary components, RSU grants and vesting\nrows, and growth assumptions; `_models/ai_settings.py` plus\n`services/ai_settings.py` for provider, model, key envelope and token budgets;\nand `services/account_settings.py` for account classification. Consumers were\nrepointed at the new tables: query_helpers, anomalies, net_worth, recurring,\ntrends, the AI tool implementations, the preferences routers, auth_service and\nledger_dimensions.\n\nFour chained revisions land it, ending in an explicit cutover:\naccount_settings_2026, ai_settings_2026, compensation_records_2026, then\ndomain_storage_cutover_2026. The chain resolves to exactly one head across all\n55 revisions, and CI now runs the new migration tests in the PostgreSQL\nintegration job, because a dialect difference passes on SQLite and fails in\nproduction.\n\nDocuments the result in docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA_REFERENCE.md, a JSON companion,\nand a DDL snapshot, with the design and verification notes under docs/plans/\nand docs/research/.\n\nAlso fixes the schema reference''s provenance record. As a path-keyed map,\n`source_files_sha256` paired a credential-looking key with a high-entropy value\nwhenever the path contained auth or token, so SonarCloud reported seven BLOCKER\nhard-coded-secret findings and an E security rating. The values are file\ndigests, confirmed by recomputing sha256 over auth_service.py. Restructured to\na list of {path, sha256} objects, verified lossless across all 129 pairs.\n\nGitignores backend/.pytest_tmp/, the scratch SQLite directory the new\nmigration tests build, which was untracked but unignored.\n\nVerified: 1585 backend tests pass with 205 skipped, ruff and mypy clean, and\nthe Sonar gate green with security rating A and zero vulnerabilities.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrI1hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQK0QAAc10ApSAVbuGjbXhbi/YVZ/\nld+MIaJ986uhmihW1FrQ2QiuYbSsTpcctZDkPlJxw0/ZjpLlsTJJMpSoWq97lvv/\nMU+4Jq5LvZuwEVxkEBIJ+XhYEIR+xPPkLycV616tKER0uXcJhw58m1c8NSwiLGV0\na7VyOMQ39aoNGh+MAdFi2I4QYA5KF3fZaSq2cejsU7BrnaL2KlA6ZgoiDt4aDrD8\nAow6HRmIvv6/Cf3hJ0ylw29JAKl9dHxKuyYWKLtd1BucMwfjMY/miNbm9NjKChn0\n+daSpBhU2wPvr0rx9tb1R8j5uJY9L3mh6DFZEbpL3jB0rSJtlG0bq2Q2bgLutpnu\nMQtwk+wW5lOrhFO63K4vbqunRMLpTZKUbIR4MDqYakq9EDjvUw/7/d5p0Ma1OgLd\nm3A3M+akb3h/DUO65Yf9C6lg+zUsb3Z7JAmNq80mnCdpo+3/mXvb/a/enL04dNzB\nUZmKwYXfnonVdm3THQHC+RQCqgv+9Y8E6Jg+5EJzgf+oP79FraFjBRqCDHDaqDrv\nc7YryQorCYEn6VgOUcplV+7Xj/uPNPcEGq6d+pQNuk1i9K/ixnyJ105ABduBNCih\nb/SRvLgBFZ0xhfYWkXbdci2x/Wm39ovlgqtzLzA9+K/SCaV/ibXaq42b3mr10aab\ng1tmBVo4LbKvqdjt/4P/\n=g52G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T01:01:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url