m/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/c6114ffce916abdd426beefa679a5d455a22915e","node_id":"C_kwDOQ2vxg9oAKGM2MTE0ZmZjZTkxNmFiZGQ0MjZiZWVmYTY3OWE1ZDQ1NWEyMjkxNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/cb0e3ec6432304c81afc384ab9a0f1b6e695ac30","sha":"cb0e3ec6432304c81afc384ab9a0f1b6e695ac30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/cb0e3ec6432304c81afc384ab9a0f1b6e695ac30"}],"sha":"c6114ffce916abdd426beefa679a5d455a22915e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/c6114ffce916abdd426beefa679a5d455a22915e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/cb0e3ec6432304c81afc384ab9a0f1b6e695ac30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:48:42Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:48:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add chart ranges, withholding summary, and recurring accuracy work (#247)\n\nChart range controls (`useChartRange` + `ChartRangeControls`) let time-series\ncharts scope to a window instead of always rendering the whole series, wired\nthrough the analytics, tax, net-worth, investment, GST and trends charts.\n`lib/chartDateLabels.ts` centralises chart date parsing so labels no longer\nrely on the browser''s ambiguous Date(string) handling of a bare YYYY-MM.\n\n`WithholdingSummary` reports cash payroll withholding, RSU share withholding\nand the combined estimate on the tax page. Missing RSU actuals fall back to a\n31.2% estimate (30% tax plus 4% cess on the tax), the standard flat perquisite\nwithholding, and the component labels it as an estimate rather than recorded\nfact. Unrecorded payroll TDS renders a placeholder with an aria-label instead\nof a zero that would read as \"no tax withheld\".\n\n`lib/finance/analysisPeriod.ts` derives the earning window from actual earning\nevidence and completed months only, so health and income figures stop being\ncomputed across partial or pre-earning periods. Backend recurring detection\nand next-expected logic updated with a new acceptance suite.\n\nAlso: profile modal split into focused row components, Money and chart\ntooltip/default refinements, doc updates, and four Archify diagrams as JSON\nspecs plus committed SVGs.\n\nThe generated HTML viewers are deliberately NOT committed. Four near-identical\n15,000-line viewers are ~60,000 lines of generated markup that SonarCloud read\nas new code, scoring 93.3% duplication against a 3% gate and carrying every\nreliability finding in the project. They are gitignored build output now,\nregenerated with `node docs/diagrams/build.mjs`. That also exposed two repairs:\n`build.mjs --check` no longer hard-fails when the viewer is absent, and the\ngenerated SVGs are excluded from the trailing-whitespace hook because a\ndelivery receipt that pins sha256 cannot survive a formatter.\n\nVerified: 1056 backend tests, 2049 frontend tests across 184 files, ruff and\nmypy clean, eslint and tsc clean, Sonar gate OK with duplication at 0.0% and\nreliability A.","tree":{"sha":"b78a6c0dddea2cc555c465f18dbf2358e515abf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/b78a6c0dddea2cc555c465f18dbf2358e515abf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/cb0e3ec6432304c81afc384ab9a0f1b6e695ac30","verification":{"payload":"tree b78a6c0dddea2cc555c465f18dbf2358e515abf3\nparent a3a0958edcda2c1e03b4e8d7e3cb30a6dcc55997\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1789562922 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789562922 +0530\n\nfeat: add chart ranges, withholding summary, and recurring accuracy work (#247)\n\nChart range controls (`useChartRange` + `ChartRangeControls`) let time-series\ncharts scope to a window instead of always rendering the whole series, wired\nthrough the analytics, tax, net-worth, investment, GST and trends charts.\n`lib/chartDateLabels.ts` centralises chart date parsing so labels no longer\nrely on the browser''s ambiguous Date(string) handling of a bare YYYY-MM.\n\n`WithholdingSummary` reports cash payroll withholding, RSU share withholding\nand the combined estimate on the tax page. Missing RSU actuals fall back to a\n31.2% estimate (30% tax plus 4% cess on the tax), the standard flat perquisite\nwithholding, and the component labels it as an estimate rather than recorded\nfact. Unrecorded payroll TDS renders a placeholder with an aria-label instead\nof a zero that would read as \"no tax withheld\".\n\n`lib/finance/analysisPeriod.ts` derives the earning window from actual earning\nevidence and completed months only, so health and income figures stop being\ncomputed across partial or pre-earning periods. Backend recurring detection\nand next-expected logic updated with a new acceptance suite.\n\nAlso: profile modal split into focused row components, Money and chart\ntooltip/default refinements, doc updates, and four Archify diagrams as JSON\nspecs plus committed SVGs.\n\nThe generated HTML viewers are deliberately NOT committed. Four near-identical\n15,000-line viewers are ~60,000 lines of generated markup that SonarCloud read\nas new code, scoring 93.3% duplication against a 3% gate and carrying every\nreliability finding in the project. They are gitignored build output now,\nregenerated with `node docs/diagrams/build.mjs`. That also exposed two repairs:\n`build.mjs --check` no longer hard-fails when the viewer is absent, and the\ngenerated SVGs are excluded from the trailing-whitespace hook because a\ndelivery receipt that pins sha256 cannot survive a formatter.\n\nVerified: 1056 backend tests, 2049 frontend tests across 184 files, ruff and\nmypy clean, eslint and tsc clean, Sonar gate OK with duplication at 0.0% and\nreliability A.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqpAqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8BcQAC4jg7sf7FmceB2O+6BJtOKe\niMFq2vM6IruA370SXpsRXKSMhfYBq9hMrFghXuIG3h9EmjBRBLQl65l7n73j43Yd\n+gN8W1Yu63AAma1X1tzI4AOpKewm99V7WKrP1UQBy7J3b7kXCsgwZlFXCi3GPzay\n/NxGEU+4kAvhQN0XEK/Rkn1fUkoOmkmeMjla4vMcnrBn4icODO2txuBkouB/SJD1\naCgBOiNzKzEF9s67XZcrT+GsUOeKRpXyAUyiytyFD8RxOFm8t54LGLQqAsyt3uSc\nq3nUDGbeNyNLWJaDfsJNjkMd5JOSJb2my9bGe4RUq7jSrGpRsaUrcISinDhT1Uqq\nbfSlC2pB7xZRhQQvrHVJn1YhMekwLNQW9zQoGrvxvRTg7oL+Lg3WtFWkiNY65DCk\nrO03hvUx3PBoLt5cs27xU0wh8zyqL5YFUOi09B3XndSBt8Ij/cJiOiv3ck/hs2Oz\nOOsi0SMmSSqKRMKnsxBAbgQty5QHtDjYGAidTwWItL06ZFfS2vCH+VdFjTz/4loe\n8BYFMdFOukaczW98ijbj9Fr529bvaF+JptoD+iwJftyvs7XfdU8O6O6q+GuAFyz/\nicxn6Rv+7DA7hvhDxBzl9RYlbaZhLg4KOs2dPbVMKGLoVN3g6QrditkHpcUwD/FK\nPNqAau4FBSe1mviPM3iu\n=rGGp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T