://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/df585875ba1ab409eede33fdc667a0e780423c26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T03:41:38Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T03:41:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(renovate): pause major updates until typescript-eslint catches up (#243)\n\nSupersedes the narrower typescript hold. That hold worked, and #241 then failed on\ntypescript-eslint''s own major behaviour instead: the frontend lint reports a wall\nof @typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-call errors on types it can no longer resolve.\n\nThat is the pattern. Each narrower hold surfaced the next blocked major in the\nsame grouped PR, so the monthly major stream could never go green.\n\nWorth noting the ordering here: this PR first failed on a pnpm minimumReleaseAge\nviolation for the vitest 5.0.0 family, which cleared on its own after 24h and\nrevealed typescript-eslint underneath. Two layers deep before the real blocker\nshowed.\n\nSecurity updates are unaffected: vulnerabilityAlerts runs on its own schedule and\nignores packageRules. Minor and patch updates continue normally.","tree":{"sha":"f689d8e31f3a8e8e2c45ed7f103b3e44eba5068d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/f689d8e31f3a8e8e2c45ed7f103b3e44eba5068d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/df585875ba1ab409eede33fdc667a0e780423c26","verification":{"payload":"tree f689d8e31f3a8e8e2c45ed7f103b3e44eba5068d\nparent 3b3d7d26a1a83d203c138faa165b0a0d2430362e\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1788666098 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788666098 +0530\n\nchore(renovate): pause major updates until typescript-eslint catches up (#243)\n\nSupersedes the narrower typescript hold. That hold worked, and #241 then failed on\ntypescript-eslint''s own major behaviour instead: the frontend lint reports a wall\nof @typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-call errors on types it can no longer resolve.\n\nThat is the pattern. Each narrower hold surfaced the next blocked major in the\nsame grouped PR, so the monthly major stream could never go green.\n\nWorth noting the ordering here: this PR first failed on a pnpm minimumReleaseAge\nviolation for the vitest 5.0.0 family, which cleared on its own after 24h and\nrevealed typescript-eslint underneath. Two layers deep before the real blocker\nshowed.\n\nSecurity updates are unaffected: vulnerabilityAlerts runs on its own schedule and\nignores packageRules. Minor and patch updates continue normally.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnODyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX54QAEVv71YheYXrTi35Or411k8N\nmbSMBdTiD9c3TCWl11Jai/AUIzpEhyMzFTPKEY8zgmsRVM034u4hhK0sRZqzmOH4\nUNA8FYmWEhD4ogJHpxzUl9mVPBxcCokDs8boH0d5SgaB1yqmI6rADYbnFVd7gidC\noZhyJDi6jWRgrxEYB+JSAkP2cOH8NBsNpA4SDhh9Xts8EyGP84+IzGAwRVKdOUtp\nu84tYcy/Q7MyJF3BHKiWbGbn+55S2tkfyxpY7FrmHMviA/5J4ZRIeR7ekebSlZeA\nZfleNJtZ0U48zjrddOMAKrJxevWNjOcyRWVwPGyfu1U+RmeTH+nStO0Py4AYxxB2\nwQ+AO2+ayU4WMJE7XT