{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/3b3d7d26a1a83d203c138faa165b0a0d2430362e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T03:17:15Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T03:17:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(renovate): hold typescript below 7 until typescript-eslint supports it (#242)\n\nThe grouped major PR (#241) fails the frontend build with ''typescript-eslint does\nnot support TS 7.0''. typescript-eslint 8.69.0 declares peerDependencies typescript\n''>=4.8.4 <6.1.0'', so it rejects 7 outright. frontend/package.json depends on\ntypescript-eslint ^8.65.0 directly.\n\nWorth recording: a pnpm minimumReleaseAge violation on the vitest 5.0.0 family was\nmasking this. Once those packages aged past the 24h cutoff and the job re-ran, the\ntypescript-eslint failure was what actually surfaced.\n\nHolding just typescript lets Renovate regenerate the monthly major PR without it,\nso the remaining majors stop being blocked behind one upstream gap. The rule\ncarries its removal condition in its description.","tree":{"sha":"3d4c417e1bb788fbd486af72b7fbeed1ac518357","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/3d4c417e1bb788fbd486af72b7fbeed1ac518357"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/3b3d7d26a1a83d203c138faa165b0a0d2430362e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d4c417e1bb788fbd486af72b7fbeed1ac518357\nparent 30e18751219838c517c9314a4d41d779db9d5be7\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1788664635 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788664635 +0530\n\nchore(renovate): hold typescript below 7 until typescript-eslint supports it (#242)\n\nThe grouped major PR (#241) fails the frontend build with ''typescript-eslint does\nnot support TS 7.0''. typescript-eslint 8.69.0 declares peerDependencies typescript\n''>=4.8.4 <6.1.0'', so it rejects 7 outright. frontend/package.json depends on\ntypescript-eslint ^8.65.0 directly.\n\nWorth recording: a pnpm minimumReleaseAge violation on the vitest 5.0.0 family was\nmasking this. Once those packages aged past the 24h cutoff and the job re-ran, the\ntypescript-eslint failure was what actually surfaced.\n\nHolding just typescript lets Renovate regenerate the monthly major PR without it,\nso the remaining majors stop being blocked behind one upstream gap. The rule\ncarries its removal condition in its description.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnNs7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXkEQAJj6zeXUty5OzHD8pPnmqQ0k\nO1ABdm9Eo96tPMb/KTv3eS/XeQAX+QdKx9UsE7El8+JkHVbDgwartys/PxjnX96F\nT16DNgY40VJ5TmPqfls+vGPGidEoL4JVo+rp3uZGZpktZAySFKPeV3aeaDl+2d1H\nTPeOkNJVzDjJKTYNtioqSfIp1vAbBej4loisjvzKkxH/as21rvCxr+4dv4jyEZnR\nkRdMK1SYCJZw0fM/lmOpZMOzEsbC6MvEnqR9ID4mXT6P0zpmd4WpX8U6HAdyQRvM\n8xARbx1TQYsg8Jeqrjc9Tz++4Sp4AVDRzfDGRfCDSEssty1XtJF0FSesyZjR2s1n\nEFU5oEZ9sQm1r1yiD0VFrDqOI6TYTtxtPEp75Qwu4z/bej15MKlnsFsD35yBYi