line,\nso GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 cannot be closed by a version bump and dependabot\nalert 105 stays open by decision. Worktrees belong at the repo root, since\nnested under frontend/ they give typescript-eslint two tsconfig roots.\nbackend/ledger_sync.db is the LOCAL dev database, not production, and the\ntwo diverged during this session.\n\nAlso replaces the stale \"~6,768 rows\" figure with \"~7,000 and growing\".\n\nCame out of auditing the Claude config set against reality: ten of eleven\nfactual claims already checked out, including the 14-skill table with zero\ndrift. Documentation only, no behaviour change. Line endings byte-verified\nat 225 CRLF and 0 bare LF.","tree":{"sha":"4d23da8c92b5410d578d701588843048b340fccf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/4d23da8c92b5410d578d701588843048b340fccf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/d4dca1d835dc7522cee5ddd955b6f1b51930cf4b","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d23da8c92b5410d578d701588843048b340fccf\nparent da88f751117067495219bf0db9794f704676ab73\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1786864305 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786864305 +0530\n\ndocs: record the toolchain traps that cost real debugging time (#235)\n\nAdds a Toolchain Gotchas section to the repo CLAUDE.md for things that are\ninvisible until they bite, each verified rather than recalled.\n\nThis repo is CRLF (core.autocrlf=true, no .gitattributes; 75 of 80 sampled\nsource files), so sed -i and Python read_text/write_text both normalize to\nLF and produce a diff touching every line. Reproduced while writing the\nsection: a Python rewrite stripped all 217 CRLF from CLAUDE.md and had to\nbe reverted. backend/uv.lock is legitimately LF at HEAD, so check a file''s\nown baseline before \"fixing\" it.\n\ntypescript-eslint 8.65.0 declares peer typescript >=4.8.4 <6.1.0 and\nhard-errors on TS 7, which breaks lint repo-wide and therefore CI, so\nTypeScript is pinned at 6.0.3 