,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/38036b19a375f979c18a27f03fc15398a6a9d441/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:09:23Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T16:09:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(rsu): convert vest-date prices at vest-date FX and record net shares (#232)\n\nThe RSU vest-date stock price was fetched historically but converted at\nTODAY''s FX rate. Verified end to end against both upstreams: AMZN closed\nat $231.03 on 2025-08-15 with USD/INR at 87.46 then against 95.34 on\n2026-08-03, so the vested line read Rs 1,32,158 instead of Rs 1,21,235 --\na 9% overstatement from currency drift alone, on a row labelled\n\"Vest-date price\" for a rupee figure that never existed on the vest date.\n\nNot display-only: Indian RSU perquisite value is fixed at vesting and\ndoes not move with later FX, and these grants drive the tax projection\nand the TDS schedule.\n\n`GET /api/exchange-rates` now takes an optional `on_date`, served by\nfrankfurter''s dated endpoint. Historical lookups deliberately bypass both\nthe 24h cache and the fallback table: a past ECB rate never changes so a\nTTL is meaningless, and the fallback is a single present-day snapshot\nwhose use for a 2025 date would silently reintroduce this exact bug. A\nfailed lookup errors instead, leaving the price unconverted so the row\nhonestly keeps showing \"Current price\". The response reports the date\nactually priced, which precedes the request across a weekend. Retries\nonce, because the dated endpoint returned Cloudflare 520/522\nintermittently while /latest stayed healthy.\n\nAdds an optional `net_quantity` per vesting for sell-to-cover, where the\nemployer withholds part of the vest to pay tax. Reporting only:\nperquisite value is taxed on the full vest, the withheld shares ARE the\ntax payment, so `quantity` remains the basis in splitRsuTotals, the\nprojection calculator and the TDS schedule. A test asserts the totals are\nidentical with and without it.\n\nAlso constrains the exchange-rate `base` parameter to a three-letter\ncurrency code. It was an unbounded string echoed into two log lines, one\nof which predates this change, so a newline-bearing value could forge a\nlog record.\n\nVerified: 844 backend tests, 1427 frontend across 121 files, ruff and\nmypy clean, lint 0 errors, SonarCloud gate OK with 0 new issues.","tree":{"sha":"fa73d85ed0bfef7eab4d8988d2f35b6e781a0e33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/fa73d85ed0bfef7eab4d8988d2f35b6e781a0e33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/38036b19a375f979c18a27f03fc15398a6a9d441","verification":{"payload":"tree fa73d85ed0bfef7eab4d8988d2f35b6e781a0e33\nparent ed078207438711afbd5f2a9bbb0e12791bbc7cbd\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1785773363 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785773363 +0530\n\nfix(rsu): convert vest-date prices at vest-date FX and record net shares (#232)\n\nThe RSU vest-date stock price was fetched historically but converted at\nTODAY''s FX rate. Verified end to end against both upstreams: AMZN closed\nat $231.03 on 2025-08-15 with USD/INR at 87.46 then against 95.34 on\n2026-08-03, so the vested line read Rs 1,32,158 instead of Rs 1,21,235 --\na 9% overstatement from currency drift alone, on a row labelled\n\"Vest-date price\" for a rupee figure that never existed on the vest date.\n\nNot display-only: Indian RSU perquisite value is fixed at vesting and\ndoes not move with later FX, and these grants drive the tax projection\nand the TDS schedule.\n\n`GET /api/exchange-rates` now takes an optional `on_date`, served by\nfrankfurter''s dated endpoint. Historical lookups deliberately bypass both\nthe 24h cache and the fallback table: a past ECB rate never changes so a\nTTL is meaningless, and the fallback is a single present-day snapshot\nwhose use for a 2025 date would silently reintroduce this exact bug. A\nfailed lookup errors instead, leaving the price unconverted so the row\nhonestly keeps showing \"Current price\". The response reports the date\nactually priced, which precedes the request across a weekend. Retries\nonce, because the dated endpoint returned Cloudflare 520/522\nintermittently while /latest stayed healthy.\n\nAdds an optional `net_quantity` per vesting for sell-to-cover, where the\nemployer withholds part of the vest to pay tax. Reporting only:\nperquisite value is taxed on the full vest, the withheld shares ARE the\ntax payment, so `quantity` remains the basis in splitRsuTotals, the\nprojection calculator and the TDS schedule. A test asserts the totals are\nidentical with and without it.\n\nAlso constrains the exchange-rate `base` parameter to a three-letter\ncurrency code. It was an unbounded string echoed into two log lines, one\nof which predates this change, so a newline-bearing value could forge a\nlog record.\n\nVerified: 844 backend tests, 1427 frontend across 121 files, ruff and\nmypy clean, lint 0 errors, SonarCloud gate OK with 0 new issues.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcL0zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYR4QAImwq34ZBB2xrwropZt6ndr1\nW/cuODLMtewGM/ikMKWI2Ixew0oQ8x9lQU1j2k2hnfHts9kiJ/R7FlcPp1InaOLI\nUi6zgBz78M5aS8oa/DCmfqZQ6y1D4HOukVXs9fdb5tGCK348vyS3/tH48E8Fc03R\nSC1lpkYEwuBkQebtBWeC7izHJZfl52pjjDo5L3SAGLtpbtqdo3sFWOJ/QQGEIVAr\nNX+Vd44mmtyYxU5qcOnYSDiRsaDCDGq/P7ImanLJDL5CJYn49g+UtdG+jm/Sn8tJ\nEh0DwUYA4Lq1pcqXtid4D9hjek/KxcWnJK/pp70FK4L1aVca9u08Yhe9HKZtvQyM\nyZXlH/wRG3Eveg0kAOGOsZZ+EFdf9p6toT6gaRrJvLunoUS8EVot8zehC6/A39kL\ndqNbc1bd2OuwE+sEfg1NC5smeLHBHyn5KQ/BsKinJ5mX5OZZyPWJOh+tVs/kh8Bo\nLZe+7//oQtlmv0nCfaM5vGD85lsStd5kBdJ2mrUrpjKicuwyBJBJBCZkQd9WZv7t\n92WfE05GUteiRXLPSBDA4uAtJwird0LYjSjZXQwaMH8iyRBTjtmsx51UBp/+ePPs\ny+vi9k3CBhdCPKibg8AdmLGfJHcntJ+N6I2DHOQ4omvNbTSfLtgw/X/00B/vLe3T\nEJ4H/Hgt8Lu7mT+oPdkG\n=lWB0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T16:09:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/38036b19a375f979c18a27f03fc15398a6a9d441","node_id":"C_kwDOQ2vxg9oAKDM4MDM2YjE5YTM3NWY5NzljMThhMjdmMDNmYzE1Mzk4YTZhOWQ0NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/ed078207438711afbd5f2a9bbb0e12791bbc7cbd","sha":"ed078207438711afbd5f2a9bbb0e12791bbc7cbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/ed078207438711afbd5f2a9bbb0e12791bbc7cbd"}],"sha":"38036b19a375f979c18a27f03fc15398a6a9d441","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/38036b19a375f979c18a27f03fc15398a6a9d441"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/ed078207438711afbd5f2a9bbb0e12791bbc7cbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T10:21:44Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T10:21:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): update dependencies, name the TDS regime, and widen prefetch (#231)\n\nCommits the dependency bumps that had been sitting uncommitted in the\nworking tree: backend lock (boto3 1.43.62, cryptography 50.0.0), and\nfrontend axios 1.19.0, vite 8.2.0, eslint 10.8.0, jsdom 30.0.1,\nrecharts 3.10.1, postcss 8.5.25, plus type and plugin bumps.\n\nTwo upgrades are deliberately excluded, each verified rather than assumed.\nTypeScript stays on 6.0.3 because typescript-eslint 8.65.0 declares peer\n`typescript: >=4.8.4 <6.1.0` and hard-errors on TS 7, which breaks lint\nrepo-wide and CI gates on lint. react-router-dom stays on 7.18.1 because\nGHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 is only patched in react-router 8.3.0 and\nreact-router-dom has no 8.x line at all -- the fix is a framework\nmigration, and main''s 7.18.1 is equally affected (dependabot alert 105).\nThe app renders a client-side BrowserRouter with no RSC APIs, so the\nadvisory does not apply either way.\n\nNames the regime behind the Cash Flow tax branch''s computed at-source\nfigure. That number is slab-derived, not a ledger row, and on this ledger\nevery FY has zero explicit tax rows while employment income is ~97% of\ninflow, so the computed figure IS the whole Tax branch.\n\nWarms seven more queries at login. Three are read by the persistent\nchrome on every page (sidebar badge, mobile tab bar, notification bell,\nStaleAnalyticsAlert), so they cut a round-trip from the whole workspace''s\nfirst paint rather than one route. Params are copied from call sites\nbecause every key factory folds its filters into the key and staleTime is\nInfinity: a prefetch off by one field pays the round-trip and still spins.\n\nVerified: 825 backend tests, 1424 frontend tests across 121 files, lint 0\nerrors, production build with PWA service worker.","tree":{"sha":"5b8f679b99c3f1f1eb7ca2060f05e8b3949ab508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/5b8f679b99c3f1f1eb7ca2060f05e8b3949ab508"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/ed078207438711afbd5f2a9bbb0e12791bbc7cbd","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b8f679b99c3f1f1eb7ca2060f05e8b3949ab508\nparent 941041a0ac9d3c211274c0633f3cca024b93d951\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1785752504 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785752504 +0530\n\nchore(deps): update dependencies, name the TDS regime, and widen prefetch (#231)\n\nCommits the dependency bumps that had been sitting uncommitted in the\nworking tree: backend lock (boto3 1.43.62, cryptography 50.0.0), and\nfrontend axios 1.19.0, vite 8.2.0, eslint 10.8.0, jsdom 30.0.1,\nrecharts 3.10.1, postcss 8.5.25, plus type and plugin bumps.\n\nTwo upgrades are deliberately excluded, each verified rather than assumed.\nTypeScript stays on 6.0.3 because typescript-eslint 8.65.0 declares peer\n`typescript: >=4.8.4 <6.1.0` and hard-errors on TS 7, which breaks lint\nrepo-wide and CI gates on lint. react-router-dom stays on 7.18.1 because\nGHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 is only patched in react-router 8.3.0 and\nreact-router-dom has no 8.x line at all -- the fix is a framework\nmigration, and main''s 7.18.1 is equally affected (dependabot alert 105).\nThe app renders a client-side BrowserRouter with no RSC APIs, so the\nadvisory does not apply either way.\n\nNames the regime behind the Cash Flow tax branch''s computed at-source\nfigure. That number is slab-derived, not a ledger row, and on this ledger\nevery FY has zero explicit tax rows while employment income is ~97% of\ninflow, so the computed figure IS the whole Tax branch.\n\nWarms seven more queries at login. Three are read by the persistent\nchrome on every page (sidebar badge, mobile tab bar, notification bell,\nStaleAnalyticsAlert), so they cut a round-trip from the whole workspace''s\nfirst paint rather than one route. Params are copied from call sites\nbecause every key factory folds its filters into the key and staleTime is\nInfinity: a prefetch off by one field pays the round-trip and still spins.\n\nVerified: 825 backend tests, 1424 frontend tests across 121 files, lint 0\nerrors, production build with PWA service worker."