tes, guards a null goal start date, and cuts 2.23.0\nwith every doc realigned against measured code.\n\nDocs pass re-derived route counts, test counts, OpenAPI totals, the migration\nhead, and the pnpm/Node versions from the code rather than carrying prior\nclaims forward. Also corrected four stale behavior claims: system theme mode,\nthe motion package rename, Vercel ASGI serving versus Mangum, and the sidebar\ngrouping.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZ2omCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUgwQAEisSv9bcqz5oPj6dv58eSGO\nHifzlnl9Q/fev+Xj3LyzMxL+32fwsAjjsWCEj3OuvZU4zjux7Lo+NpjABdI1eRp5\nwBmDz5JQbUlOMusj25Rf8LVvA6DF+SUnMtFxrwMZ42H9165GgT3jAUXJtjghEfTA\nKzTgj71qASMxh/LpoxWuzfYyd5owHdwP3ZyejfS1adlc83K2dBRBpassCcbHT0G7\nm2xqvG+owWjqdAI6S4PJ5Y7YJBBViKYedsB2s1TySS9Ge3nUM7WZ1mCE2o7JN2dx\naXh56U6lKxzMVhd8JNIjdIumA3r+5vLklRIWS1KeEo4QzMpad2/wIsTK10CWUmJ9\nziQe7IaRxsYe4bID8biDjb+1DQCOyPMOPAdGsm9aBDPQpK6tpDBEpi/xISSZYJNn\nFU6yd51gPW+aq49m2d7W8/10meE4wmr4X4pVh9M8LsrXH7YeJK/Dr0rnX9vI5L1p\nhrtZiYRMfqZU6jl6QIyakM5CGVfgfujJFUBavfYZQzQCob58S+maJT9Y6cAVO1ZX\n1/fUPNfqZJIVW6Fl1oNuCRDtSQQxGW0ce/5KTHhn63cozCkzS7R76JsXfa0qZhha\neSJKH1zfxy3WDiFhUb71WffUMkc2ZPxFzBhJWiWcG2z9/debadz9yaef3hhO+I+T\n2l+eLFirp9Zi84+XBT4b\n=fblu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T14:24:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/fe27a5159d6bc2b22a81a7cd99daad52ee2982a0","node_id":"C_kwDOQ2vxg9oAKGZlMjdhNTE1OWQ2YmMyYjIyYTgxYTdjZDk5ZGFhZDUyZWUyOTgyYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2","sha":"d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2"}],"sha":"fe27a5159d6bc2b22a81a7cd99daad52ee2982a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/fe27a5159d6bc2b22a81a7cd99daad52ee2982a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:08:35Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:39:10Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"message":"fix(db): make alembic upgrade head work against an empty database\n\n`uv run alembic upgrade head` on a fresh database failed at the first\n`batch_op.drop_index(op.f(\"ix_fy_summaries_fiscal_year\"))`: the migration\nthat creates `fy_summaries` names its index `ix_fy_summary_year`, so the\ndrop had nothing to drop and batch-mode reflection raised. Nothing caught\nit -- CI never ran migrations from scratch, prod only applies new revisions\nto a Neon database that already carries the history, and `init_db()`''s\n`create_all()` masks migration gaps at runtime.\n\nFixing the reported drop exposed three more breaks in the same class, all\nfrom the same root cause (migrations were never the complete schema):\n\n- `account_classifications` was created by no migration at all, only by\n  `create_all()`. Added guarded on reflection, following the existing\n  `_create_transactions_table_if_missing` precedent.\n- af63e055055a used non-batch `create_foreign_key` / `create_unique_constraint`,\n  which SQLite cannot do, and dropped four more create_all-named indexes.\n- The rollup backfill selected preference columns that only `create_all()`\n  ever added. It now returns early when there are no users, since there is\n  nothing to repair on a fresh database.\n\nReaching head was not enough on its own: the resulting schema still lacked\n12 columns the ORM requires, so the app would fail on `no such column:\npayday`. A reconciliation revision adds them, every add guarded on\nreflection so it is a no-op on deployed databases. Verified against a\ncreate_all-shaped database stamped at the old head: the incremental path\napplies one revision, drift goes to zero, and rows are preserved.\n\nNo applied migration''s effect is changed -- drops became conditional and\nconstraint DDL moved into batch mode, both no-ops where the objects\nalready exist as before.\n\nRegression coverage, whose absence is why this survived: an integration\ntest upgrades a temp empty database and asserts it reaches head, that the\nschema has every ORM table and column, and that re-running is idempotent.\nConfirmed to fail with the original `No such index` error when the\nmigration fixes are reverted. Wired the same from-scratch upgrade into\nci.yml so every PR proves it.","tree":{"sha":"91df478762e2ac0ed7fafd6658dc6a35776997e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/91df478762e2ac0ed7fafd6658dc6a35776997e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2","node_id":"C_kwDOQ2vxg9oAKGQ3MTUyYmQyOTlkNGY1NGM5MmU0YzViNDAxY2IxOTE3MTgzZGI2YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c","sha":"f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c"}],"sha":"d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/d7152bd299d4f54c92e4c5b401cb1917183db6a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T11:52:13Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:28:31Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"message":"fix: score each savings numerator against its own target\n\n/budgets and /spending-analysis both read savings_target_percent while\ncomputing different savings numerators. /budgets measures the net change\nin the investment perimeter; /spending-analysis measures income minus\nexpenses. On the real ledger for FY2025-26 those are 578,428.79 and\n1,182,355.68, so one 20% floor let /budgets report \"under target\" while\n/spending-analysis reported \"on track\" for the same user in the same\nperiod. Both columns default to 20.0, which kept the mismatch silent.\n\nThe numerators are deliberate and stay separate (see savingsRate.ts).\nThe target is what needed splitting, and the field already exists:\nsavings_goal_percent is the app''s income-minus-expenses target, already\nscored against exactly that quantity by the Financial Health savings\nmetric and the Trends savings-rate goal line. /spending-analysis was the\nonly income-minus-expenses surface reaching for the allocation target\ninstead, so it now reads savings_goal_percent and savings_target_percent\nstays the /budgets allocation floor. No new column, no migration, and no\nexisting setting changes meaning.\n\nNeeds + wants + savings no longer necessarily sum to 100 on\n/spending-analysis, so its heading stops printing them as a 50/30/20\ntriplet and the savings floor moves into a caption beside the definition\nit applies to. Each Savings card now names its numerator and its target,\nand both settings fields state which bar they set.","tree":{"sha":"d1d3638a95d88e6345b4f5873d291875b8bec79c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/d1d3638a95d88e6345b4f5873d291875b8bec79c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c","node_id":"C_kwDOQ2vxg9oAKGYyYWYyZTFlOTZlMTZjYTE3MWFjMWY2N2YxMDhjMzNkYzkwMmZiN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474","sha":"e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474"}],"sha":"f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/f2af2e1e96e16ca171ac1f67f108c33dc902fb7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:16:00Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T12:27:01Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"message":"refactor(frontend): drop deprecated bare-total buffering overload\n\nFinishes the migration the TODO in ageOfMoneyCalculator was tracking, so\nS1874 and S1135 clear together.\n\nDashboardPage now builds its spendable pool with computeLiquidPosition\ninstead of summing a bare total behind a local LIQUID_CLASSIFICATIONS\nset, and passes the resulting LiquidPosition to computeDaysOfBuffering.\nThe number-taking overload and its TODO are gone, so a bare total is now\na compile error (TS2345) rather than a silently wrong reading.\n\nThis CHANGES a displayed figure: Days of Buffering on the Dashboard\ndrops, because the split-aware path excludes parked deposits and\nsubtracts debt the bare total could not see.\n\nAdds a regression guard that pins both exclusions independently -- a\nparked deposit and a negative card balance must each move the result, so\nreintroducing the bare-total path (or faking a position with\nliabilities: 0) goes red.","tree":{"sha":"43e6b52c39e3fb46ba617fc0431d4fddeaf0a51b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/43e6b52c39e3fb46ba617fc0431d4fddeaf0a51b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474","node_id":"C_kwDOQ2vxg9oAKGUyNTgyMzY4YjIyYWRmNmE1ZWE1OGIyNTIxMTM5NzQ2ZTE0OGU0NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2","sha":"6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2"}],"sha":"e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/e2582368b22adf6a5ea58b2521139746e148e474"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:47:04Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T10:47:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: product review v2.23 -- money math, API contract drift, IST clock, static analysis (#225)\n\n* fix(analytics): rebuild merchant extraction from notes\n\nThe old extractor matched a 4-regex brand whitelist and fell back to the\nnote''s first word. Measured against a real 5,015-row expense ledger that\nmatched 18.6% of rows carrying 1.9% of spend, then fragmented the rest:\n391 labels for 939 distinct notes, with ''Uber'' absorbing 101 unrelated\nnotes and ''Fruits''/''Milk''/''Egg''/''Flight'' each collapsing many purchases.\nIt also mis-attributed 13 fruit rows (''Milk Shake - Apple'', ''Fruit Bowl -\nApple/Guava'') to Apple Inc., surfaced a merchant literally named\n''Unknown'', and silently dropped lowercase or quantity-prefixed notes\n(''3* Jeans'', ''wifi bill'') worth INR 481,511.\n\nReplace it with a two-tier extractor: an expanded brand table with an\nambiguity guard, then the whole cleaned note as a descriptor rather than\none token. Brand matches for everyday words (apple, prime, orange, jio)\nrequire a supporting context token and are rejected inside food\ncategories. Placeholder notes are dropped instead of becoming merchants.\n\nCoverage on the same ledger goes to 91.8% of rows / 96.8% of spend with\nzero food rows attributed to a technology company.\n\nAlso:\n- add label_kind so consumers can tell a payee from a purchase\n  description; keying buckets on (label, kind) stops an ''Apple'' fruit row\n  merging with real Apple purchases\n- store up to 25 note variations per merchant in merchant_aliases\n- band recurrence on the median gap, not the mean, which telescoped to\n  span/(n-1) and pushed monthly merchants out of the recurring band\n- expose label_kind + aliases on /merchant-intelligence with a filter\n\n* fix(analytics): exclude in-progress periods from month comparisons\n\nThe app charted and compared the current month as if it were complete. On\n2026-07-26 the ledger held 13,511 of income against a typical 225,000, so\nthe trends page reported a savings rate of -696.8% and the comparison page\nshowed income \"down 94%\" -- both pure calendar artifacts.\n\nCentral fix, not per-page:\n- dateUtils gains addDaysToKey and inclusiveDaySpan alongside the existing\n  partial-month primitives, so no page hand-rolls day math again.\n- Trends & Forecasts runs metrics, MoM chart and breakdown table on\n  completed months only.\n- Comparison truncates BOTH spans to the same elapsed-day count in every\n  mode. Previously only FY did this, using UTC date mutation; the shared\n  alignToElapsed helper is timezone-stable and clamps when period A is the\n  shorter span.\n- PartialPeriodNotice states the exclusion on screen, since an unexplained\n  gap in a trend is its own kind of lie.\n\n37 new tests (dateUtils 41 pass, periodAlign 8 pass); full suite 374 pass,\ntypes and lint clean.\n\n* fix(recurring): classify commitments vs habits and surface detected bills\n\nTwo independent failures made the recurring feature report nothing against a\nledger full of real rent and salary.\n\nSurfacing: Subscription Tracker and the Dashboard \"Fixed Commitments\" KPI\nfiltered to is_confirmed, but nothing in the product ever set that flag, so\nthe filter matched zero rows by construction. Both now count confirmed AND\ndetected commitments, and RecurringCard gains a confirm action so the flag\ncan finally be set.\n\nPrecision: gap regularity cannot separate rent from a daily lunch, since\nboth repeat. classify_pattern_kind adds a calendar gate -- monthly-or-longer\nfrequency, >=60% of occurrences anchored to one day of the month (circular\nover a 31-day cycle), and <=25% of months containing a duplicate. Rows that\nfail it are labelled habit, and every fixed-cost, bill-calendar, and\nupcoming-payment surface filters to commitment.\n\nVerified on the real ledger: 112 patterns split into 44 commitments\n(rent, salary, EPF, tuition) and 68 habits (meals, juice, cashback).\n\n* chore(tooling): widen static analysis to 25 ruff families and a type-aware eslint tier\n\nBackend ruff select grows from 5 families to 25 (bugbear, bandit, datetimez,\ncomprehensions, pathlib, logging, and the rest). The tree is clean against all\nof them, so regressions now fail CI rather than accumulating. Each per-file\nignore carries the reason it exists instead of a bare rule code; the previous\nset ignored families that were never selected in the first place.\n\nCI lints `.` rather than `src/ tests/`, matching the documented local command,\nso CI can no longer pass on a tree where `pnpm run lint:backend` fails --\n`api/index.py` and `scripts/` were outside the linted set entirely.\n\nFrontend adds `recommendedTypeChecked` scoped to `src/**`. The syntax-only tier\ncannot see `any` flowing through a value, which is how a null request body\nreached a handler that required one and how the auth refresh interceptor came to\nread its whole payload off `any`. The two noisy-but-cosmetic rules stay at warn.\n\n* fix(backend): correct money math, add IST ledger clock, and split capital loss from consumption\n\nVerified against the real 8,181-row workbook, so every claim below is a\nreproduced defect rather than a code smell.\n\nMoney and reporting correctness:\n\n- `total_expenses` summed realised capital losses alongside consumption. A loss\n  is booked as an Expense row so the cash column balances, but it is a negative\n  investment return -- counting it as spending inflated expenses and depressed\n  the savings rate. `expense_sum_col(..., loss_keys=...)` now splits the two;\n  net savings still subtracts the loss because the cash really left.\n- `consistency_score` returned a flat 100 when a coefficient of variation was\n  undefined (fewer than two months, or a zero mean). 100 reads as the BEST\n  possible result, so a brand-new user saw a perfect score. Endpoints now ship\n  `consistency_measurable`, and `spending_velocity` ships\n  `velocity_comparable` for the same reason -- its 0 was indistinguishable from\n  \"spending is 100% down\".\n- `Refunds & Cashbacks` versus `Refunds & Cashback` key drift silently zeroed a\n  non-taxable-income bucket. Migration folds the plural variant.\n- Preference JSON defaults stored as `\"[]\"` are truthy, so the\n  essential-category defaults were dead code that never applied.\n\nTimezone class (recurring here -- FY is Apr-Mar and users are IST):\n\n- New `core/ledger_clock.py` anchors \"now\", today, and month/FY boundaries to\n  IST wall clock, matching the naive DateTime columns. Callers that compared a\n  naive ledger date against `datetime.now(UTC)` drifted by up to 5h30m, which at\n  a month or FY boundary moves a transaction into the wrong reporting period.\n\nAlso: user-scoped anomaly review, transaction export honouring its filters, a\nrow cap on `/transactions/all`, insight generation split out of `insights.py`\ninto rule and generator modules, and account-type bucketing aligned with the\n`AccountType` enum values.\n\n86 files, 807 tests passing.\n\n* fix(frontend): centralize money math, close API contract drift, add data-health and merchant pages\n\nVerified against the real 8,181-row workbook. Every item below is a reproduced\ndefect, not a code smell.\n\nMoney math, now single-source:\n\nNew `lib/savingsRate.ts` and `lib/expenseClassification.ts` replace arithmetic\nthat was re-derived per page, and the copies disagreed:\n\n- Two rates answered two different questions (\"what share of income did I keep\"\n  versus \"what share did I consume\") under one name, so two pages reported\n  different savings rates for identical rows.\n- Realised capital losses counted as consumption in some copies, not in others.\n  A loss is booked as an Expense row so cash balances, but it is a negative\n  investment return.\n- `formatPercent` takes an already-scaled 0-100 value; callers handed it\n  fractions, so anomaly deviations rendered 100x too small.\n- The 50/30/20 savings bucket is the net change in the investment PERIMETER, not\n  income minus expenses. The old definition reported money that merely sat in a\n  bank account as invested, and forced `unallocated` to zero by construction, so\n  the residual could never surface. /budget now shows it.\n- `Refunds & Cashbacks` plural key drift zeroed a whole income bucket.\n\nAPI contract drift:\n\nFastAPI silently DROPS a query param its handler does not declare -- no 422,\nHTTP 200, param discarded. A call sending one compiles, type-checks, reads like\na contract, and does nothing. `useAnalyticsV2` now derives every hook signature\nand key-factory position from the service method itself, which had drifted by 12\nparams across 10 endpoints. Live consequences:\n\n- `getKPIs` took a date window against an endpoint declaring only `time_range`,\n  so a date-filtered KPI read answered with all-time figures.\n- `getRecentTransactions` sent `sort`/`sort_order` to an endpoint declaring\n  neither, which hardcodes its own ordering; the names were not even the ones its\n  sibling `/search` uses.\n- Key positions for params the request never carried split the cache on a value\n  the server cannot see, so two callers refetched identical data under different\n  keys.\n\n`analyticsParamContract.test.ts` parses the client source itself, so that half of\nthe guard cannot fall behind. Six dead service methods, three unmounted hooks and\nthree types are gone; the endpoints stay live and the note in `analytics.ts`\nrecords why and how to re-add one. Nothing consumed `GeneratedInsight`, which is\nhow its shape drifted wrong on every field without a compile error.\n\nHonest empty and error states:\n\n- Dashboard and Data Health rendered a bare error panel on any query failure.\n- `consistency_score` and `spending_velocity` sentinels are gated on the\n  backend''s new `consistency_measurable` / `velocity_comparable` flags -- a flat\n  100 read as the best possible score for a user with one month of data.\n- `demoCalculations` account balances answered a flat shape where the endpoint\n  nests under `statistics`, and counted a zero balance as positive.\n\nNew pages: Data Health (surfaces the 29.8% category pollution the workbook\nactually has) and Merchant Intelligence (notes are 100% populated, so merchant\nextraction is viable).\n\nAlso: 10 of 13 demo cache seed keys were unreachable and are pinned by a\nround-trip contract test; `toSorted` replaced with spread-then-sort (firefox115+,\npast this repo''s firefox114 target, unpolyfilled); `AnomalyCard` renders icons\nthrough a module-level component so React updates rather than remounts.\n\n308 files, 1350 frontend tests passing.\n\n* fix(frontend): give every sort an explicit comparator\n\nA bare `.sort()` coerces elements to string and compares UTF-16 code\nunits. On the fixed-width `YYYY-MM` keys in `recentIncome.ts` that is\nright only by accident -- the sorted keys feed a `slice(-12)` that\ndecides which months count as recent income, the divisor behind the\nRecurring Coverage ratio, so a non-uniform key would silently pick the\nwrong window. Sonar gates on this as typescript:S2871.\n\nFixes the three production sites and adds a tree-wide source-scan guard\nalongside the existing utcDateKeyGuard and browserTargetBuiltins ones,\nso the next comparator-free sort fails a test instead of a quality gate.\nTest files keep bare sorts: they are set-equality comparisons on small\nstring arrays and never ship.","tree":{"sha":"fa2b4cc8861c945232f96a53bc708db46e7ac246","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/fa2b4cc8861c945232f96a53bc708db46e7ac246"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2","verification":{"payload":"tree fa2b4cc8861c945232f96a53bc708db46e7ac246\nparent 450f27f3b8c5e5fd6f5dde47e004b61f2a1bb505\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1785149224 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785149224 +0530\n\nfix: product review v2.23 -- money math, API contract drift, IST clock, static analysis (#225)\n\n* fix(analytics): rebuild merchant extraction from notes\n\nThe old extractor matched a 4-regex brand whitelist and fell back to the\nnote''s first word. Measured against a real 5,015-row expense ledger that\nmatched 18.6% of rows carrying 1.9% of spend, then fragmented the rest:\n391 labels for 939 distinct notes, with ''Uber'' absorbing 101 unrelated\nnotes and ''Fruits''/''Milk''/''Egg''/''Flight'' each collapsing many purchases.\nIt also mis-attributed 13 fruit rows (''Milk Shake - Apple'', ''Fruit Bowl -\nApple/Guava'') to Apple Inc., surfaced a merchant literally named\n''Unknown'', and silently dropped lowercase or quantity-prefixed notes\n(''3* Jeans'', ''wifi bill'') worth INR 481,511.\n\nReplace it with a two-tier extractor: an expanded brand table with an\nambiguity guard, then the whole cleaned note as a descriptor rather than\none token. Brand matches for everyday words (apple, prime, orange, jio)\nrequire a supporting context token and are rejected inside food\ncategories. Placeholder notes are dropped instead of becoming merchants.\n\nCoverage on the same ledger goes to 91.8% of rows / 96.8% of spend with\nzero food rows attributed to a technology company.\n\nAlso:\n- add label_kind so consumers can tell a payee from a purchase\n  description; keying buckets on (label, kind) stops an ''Apple'' fruit row\n  merging with real Apple purchases\n- store up to 25 note variations per merchant in merchant_aliases\n- band recurrence on the median gap, not the mean, which telescoped to\n  span/(n-1) and pushed monthly merchants out of the recurring band\n- expose label_kind + aliases on /merchant-intelligence with a filter\n\n* fix(analytics): exclude in-progress periods from month comparisons\n\nThe app charted and compared the current month as if it were complete. On\n2026-07-26 the ledger held 13,511 of income against a typical 225,000, so\nthe trends page reported a savings rate of -696.8% and the comparison page\nshowed income \"down 94%\" -- both pure calendar artifacts.\n\nCentral fix, not per-page:\n- dateUtils gains addDaysToKey and inclusiveDaySpan alongside the existing\n  partial-month primitives, so no page hand-rolls day math again.\n- Trends & Forecasts runs metrics, MoM chart and breakdown table on\n  completed months only.\n- Comparison truncates BOTH spans to the same elapsed-day count in every\n  mode. Previously only FY did this, using UTC date mutation; the shared\n  alignToElapsed helper is timezone-stable and clamps when period A is the\n  shorter span.\n- PartialPeriodNotice states the exclusion on screen, since an unexplained\n  gap in a trend is its own kind of lie.\n\n37 new tests (dateUtils 41 pass, periodAlign 8 pass); full suite 374 pass,\ntypes and lint clean.\n\n* fix(recurring): classify commitments vs habits and surface detected bills\n\nTwo independent failures made the recurring feature report nothing against a\nledger full of real rent and salary.\n\nSurfacing: Subscription Tracker and the Dashboard \"Fixed Commitments\" KPI\nfiltered to is_confirmed, but nothing in the product ever set that flag, so\nthe filter matched zero rows by construction. Both now count confirmed AND\ndetected commitments, and RecurringCard gains a confirm action so the flag\ncan finally be set.\n\nPrecision: gap regularity cannot separate rent from a daily lunch, since\nboth repeat. classify_pattern_kind adds a calendar gate -- monthly-or-longer\nfrequency, >=60% of occurrences anchored to one day of the month (circular\nover a 31-day cycle), and <=25% of months containing a duplicate. Rows that\nfail it are labelled habit, and every fixed-cost, bill-calendar, and\nupcoming-payment surface filters to commitment.\n\nVerified on the real ledger: 112 patterns split into 44 commitments\n(rent, salary, EPF, tuition) and 68 habits (meals, juice, cashback).\n\n* chore(tooling): widen static analysis to 25 ruff families and a type-aware eslint tier\n\nBackend ruff select grows from 5 families to 25 (bugbear, bandit, datetimez,\ncomprehensions, pathlib, logging, and the rest). The tree is clean against all\nof them, so regressions now fail CI rather than accumulating. Each per-file\nignore carries the reason it exists instead of a bare rule code; the previous\nset ignored families that were never selected in the first place.\n\nCI lints `.` rather than `src/ tests/`, matching the documented local command,\nso CI can no longer pass on a tree where `pnpm run lint:backend` fails --\n`api/index.py` and `scripts/` were outside the linted set entirely.\n\nFrontend adds `recommendedTypeChecked` scoped to `src/**`. The syntax-only tier\ncannot see `any` flowing through a value, which is how a null request body\nreached a handler that required one and how the auth refresh interceptor came to\nread its whole payload off `any`. The two noisy-but-cosmetic rules stay at warn.\n\n* fix(backend): correct money math, add IST ledger clock, and split capital loss from consumption\n\nVerified against the real 8,181-row workbook, so every claim below is a\nreproduced defect rather than a code smell.\n\nMoney and reporting correctness:\n\n- `total_expenses` summed realised capital losses alongside consumption. A loss\n  is booked as an Expense row so the cash column balances, but it is a negative\n  investment return -- counting it as spending inflated expenses and depressed\n  the savings rate. `expense_sum_col(..., loss_keys=...)` now splits the two;\n  net savings still subtracts the loss because the cash really left.\n- `consistency_score` returned a flat 100 when a coefficient of variation was\n  undefined (fewer than two months, or a zero mean). 100 reads as the BEST\n  possible result, so a brand-new user saw a perfect score. Endpoints now ship\n  `consistency_measurable`, and `spending_velocity` ships\n  `velocity_comparable` for the same reason -- its 0 was indistinguishable from\n  \"spending is 100% down\".\n- `Refunds & Cashbacks` versus `Refunds & Cashback` key drift silently zeroed a\n  non-taxable-income bucket. Migration folds the plural variant.\n- Preference JSON defaults stored as `\"[]\"` are truthy, so the\n  essential-category defaults were dead code that never applied.\n\nTimezone class (recurring here -- FY is Apr-Mar and users are IST):\n\n- New `core/ledger_clock.py` anchors \"now\", today, and month/FY boundaries to\n  IST wall clock, matching the naive DateTime columns. Callers that compared a\n  naive ledger date against `datetime.now(UTC)` drifted by up to 5h30m, which at\n  a month or FY boundary moves a transaction into the wrong reporting period.\n\nAlso: user-scoped anomaly review, transaction export honouring its filters, a\nrow cap on `/transactions/all`, insight generation split out of `insights.py`\ninto rule and generator modules, and account-type bucketing aligned with the\n`AccountType` enum values.\n\n86 files, 807 tests passing.\n\n* fix(frontend): centralize money math, close API contract drift, add data-health and merchant pages\n\nVerified against the real 8,181-row workbook. Every item below is a reproduced\ndefect, not a code smell.\n\nMoney math, now single-source:\n\nNew `lib/savingsRate.ts` and `lib/expenseClassification.ts` replace arithmetic\nthat was re-derived per page, and the copies disagreed:\n\n- Two rates answered two different questions (\"what share of income did I keep\"\n  versus \"what share did I consume\") under one name, so two pages reported\n  different savings rates for identical rows.\n- Realised capital losses counted as consumption in some copies, not in others.\n  A loss is booked as an Expense row so cash balances, but it is a negative\n  investment return.\n- `formatPercent` takes an already-scaled 0-100 value; callers handed it\n  fractions, so anomaly deviations rendered 100x too small.\n- The 50/30/20 savings bucket is the net change in the investment PERIMETER, not\n  income minus expenses. The old definition reported money that merely sat in a\n  bank account as invested, and forced `unallocated` to zero by construction, so\n  the residual could never surface. /budget now shows it.\n- `Refunds & Cashbacks` plural key drift zeroed a whole income bucket.\n\nAPI contract drift:\n\nFastAPI silently DROPS a query param its handler does not declare -- no 422,\nHTTP 200, param discarded. A call sending one compiles, type-checks, reads like\na contract, and does nothing. `useAnalyticsV2` now derives every hook signature\nand key-factory position from the service method itself, which had drifted by 12\nparams across 10 endpoints. Live consequences:\n\n- `getKPIs` took a date window against an endpoint declaring only `time_range`,\n  so a date-filtered KPI read answered with all-time figures.\n- `getRecentTransactions` sent `sort`/`sort_order` to an endpoint declaring\n  neither, which hardcodes its own ordering; the names were not even the ones its\n  sibling `/search` uses.\n- Key positions for params the request never carried split the cache on a value\n  the server cannot see, so two callers refetched identical data under different\n  keys.\n\n`analyticsParamContract.test.ts` parses the client source itself, so that half of\nthe guard cannot fall behind. Six dead service methods, three unmounted hooks and\nthree types are gone; the endpoints stay live and the note in `analytics.ts`\nrecords why and how to re-add one. Nothing consumed `GeneratedInsight`, which is\nhow its shape drifted wrong on every field without a compile error.\n\nHonest empty and error states:\n\n- Dashboard and Data Health rendered a bare error panel on any query failure.\n- `consistency_score` and `spending_velocity` sentinels are gated on the\n  backend''s new `consistency_measurable` / `velocity_comparable` flags -- a flat\n  100 read as the best possible score for a user with one month of data.\n- `demoCalculations` account balances answered a flat shape where the endpoint\n  nests under `statistics`, and counted a zero balance as positive.\n\nNew pages: Data Health (surfaces the 29.8% category pollution the workbook\nactually has) and Merchant Intelligence (notes are 100% populated, so merchant\nextraction is viable).\n\nAlso: 10 of 13 demo cache seed keys were unreachable and are pinned by a\nround-trip contract test; `toSorted` replaced with spread-then-sort (firefox115+,\npast this repo''s firefox114 target, unpolyfilled); `AnomalyCard` renders icons\nthrough a module-level component so React updates rather than remounts.\n\n308 files, 1350 frontend tests passing.\n\n* fix(frontend): give every sort an explicit comparator\n\nA bare `.sort()` coerces elements to string and compares UTF-16 code\nunits. On the fixed-width `YYYY-MM` keys in `recentIncome.ts` that is\nright only by accident -- the sorted keys feed a `slice(-12)` that\ndecides which months count as recent income, the divisor behind the\nRecurring Coverage ratio, so a non-uniform key would silently pick the\nwrong window. Sonar gates on this as typescript:S2871.\n\nFixes the three production sites and adds a tree-wide source-scan guard\nalongside the existing utcDateKeyGuard and browserTargetBuiltins ones,\nso the next comparator-free sort fails a test instead of a quality gate.\nTest files keep bare sorts: they are set-equality comparisons on small\nstring arrays and never ship.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZzcoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEekQAD79mOb1FXu8jX5on4qD/dDY\nNo/satJAfAdijMpz+/YOKmW0LXp/DjS+SC9bbOaTvsnWzqSNYcXlgB6KlOfFSrXJ\nhE/t9j3fbb6ccEd5cfzQ3Ma9DQ2LKDorta0MtbsNG/6cNrnL3rWogOVK+Qrnegj0\nwn31qYtBzmEGpwxWA/8FwqDhzXHD8dvkU3s7WyEvzymaVXZqs7rORjEFp8qPFhBZ\ngBeMSClDVwDIqZbrIy1Uq+yk4dbkK9uiPA4ECLcIJBrtJSwLc2x0BkCD50Gb4rUJ\nnY5YAg/mJdQ4Q/LuIXm2FT2jmhDba7JGDuyDL1Mxt6MIdYvch2YEFXg4+EM/3Rdx\na8jSrvikHalsJJfc7TyUtZfARjdcFMJ75Ss4ud1Ck/ch+DYTncyBkL0qxE1d4d1R\nH67v0OadJxcZCpujfOkyW3oiQOR/vBn6xMe8NhCo9wSdbg91HeFTHPfyt5gVin+M\ni1aVnFKh6nwhF3sH1BjGmTwnoN5L1Mpz+rzoEh7hFdrliW03DyoT3HFhsynEl/eD\nyBPmXsRA3TPsE8LVCYjTBhmro+q1PwTVgbouVmt1hbN07tCVID71LIWg7tEVnK4d\n3wVESk1i0r0BmGjPQfStvT5wmtTnXcunKIRkmpp7E8Fisb3uqVH3REWzEOUQgRv8\nQyOCcWuUho9N/ZOQQoKV\n=91WP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T10:47:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2","node_id":"C_kwDOQ2vxg9oAKDZmZmM1MDhmMjVmMzg4M2M3Y2EyYzYzMjVmNzgxMWZlOTBmMzEwZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commit/450f27f3b8c5e5fd6f5dde47e004b61f2a1bb505","sha":"450f27f3b8c5e5fd6f5dde47e004b61f2a1bb505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/450f27f3b8c5e5fd6f5dde47e004b61f2a1bb505"}],"sha":"6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/6ffc508f25f3883c7ca2c6325f7811fe90f310e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92421383?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagargupta16","id":92421383,"login":"Sagargupta16","node_id":"U_kgDOBYI9Bw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sagargupta16","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/commits/450f27f3b8c5e5fd6f5dde47e004b61f2a1bb505/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T01:44:43Z","email":"sg85207@gmail.com","name":"Sagar Gupta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T01:44:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: surface unclassified income categories in settings (#224)\n\nThe four *_income_categories preference lists are exact-match key sets and a stored non-empty list is honoured verbatim by the backend, so the shipped defaults never gap-fill a partially-configured list. An income bucket missing from all four quietly leaves every classified total, and a saved key matching no ledger row sums zero while reading as configured.\n\nAdd GET /api/calculations/income-facets (buckets with row count and sum), reconcile it against the saved lists in the Settings income section, and show both failure modes: unclassified buckets sorted by amount with a per-row bucket picker plus a bulk apply-suggestions action, and dead keys with a remove action. Suggestions reuse the same keyword rules as the first-run defaults and only ever add unclaimed buckets, so an explicitly configured list stays authoritative.","tree":{"sha":"c90e959ea7dab774c377c8eb48f14136aa32a8e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/trees/c90e959ea7dab774c377c8eb48f14136aa32a8e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Sagargupta16/ledger-sync/git/commits/450f27f3b8c5e5fd6f5dde47e004b61f2a1bb505","verification":{"payload":"tree c90e959ea7dab774c377c8eb48f14136aa32a8e2\nparent 7535b16739e64bb7c083c0d96793c4aaedbc1076\nauthor Sagar Gupta <sg85207@gmail.com> 1785116683 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785116683 +0530\n\nfeat: surface unclassified income categories in settings (#224)\n\nThe four *_income_categories preference lists are exact-match key sets and a stored non-empty list is honoured verbatim by the backend, so the shipped defaults never gap-fill a partially-configured list. An income bucket missing from all four quietly leaves every classified total, and a saved key matching no ledger row sums zero while reading as configured.\n\nAdd GET /api/calculations/income-facets (buckets with row count and sum), reconcile it against the saved lists in the Settings income section, and show both failure modes: unclassified buckets sorted by amount with a per-row bucket picker plus a bulk apply-suggestions action, and dead keys with a remove action. Suggestions reuse the same keyword rules as the first-run defaults and only ever add unclaimed buckets, so an explicitly configured list stays authoritative.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZrgLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwY4QADdmpYn2mYJxwbmoxpwVirZc\n+6r4r5l9dHySz1BEreYb6+FcmFghoqCZdFI8FLYfj96KAaGkAyt7AQlnjvuM7THx\nFuBPWuE0gc+nRg3JiU3A1nxlMzTk10wtDAaPAkAuvfkuq7ilFZylpkkhxZyOR39r\nkQZf4yMMupr5ue4dCJIQ6/sbMdJi57usQTOLFbr3eGp5ud8wZZmZ0yf1AAFDwoRr\nHktG3X3JX6zY5TuCE9B00RavpPwVjvI+fTSZH9K71Nlb3gq5UCHCQll+qw6SXECu\nqFJKHXJydDTf12l1+zJaFeutXTyTndex8EBgM+G+SMMSg5/5x7QkcjcyC4qfXcmo\nGPYzBTXRhjEipYAJH8MMrTzGEqSE6unQwkrAzkqe201ZTLcm/Tze2DJG0+0ZADBX\nohYOgoWcbb/cDe/u60EUiWCz1RrgpD18EfZY5xXrDkquY9Hj2gTo/fRorGnKJ7u/\nCRWg1l0nFSOUxGER1DpoaS69FrcFW3x1F8G9JCkqIFjNZVbqHoC4ZIjX6r+qJJLg\n1pHsVsxVoxbwmOsdlAMCMoVO8gM2Mz9WTA/PKgZ3U78HjgBtub5F9OEXRLxiJnst\nEHBvENL2cv1/AZpvkXAxwOi4nnYdL/cvzhw6WIb6GHdAmM99hZcZxXW1ACiPF7Cx\nYhxb7963vo/FMQF7PGWN\n=ULl9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-27T01:44:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/